<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose five points to 1,262.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose five points to 1,262.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,262 today from 1,257 on June 11, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1322    12.006	  1316    11.950</p>
<p>   1a   1258  9525.000	  1246  9436.000</p>
<p>   2    1484    21.206	  1474    21.057</p>
<p>   2a   1406 11531.000	  1399 11471.000</p>
<p>   3    1318    12.163	  1312    12.107</p>
<p>   3a   1152  9094.000	  1132  8936.000</p>
<p>   6    1287    13.275	  1288    13.286</p>
<p>   7    1270     6.181	  1178     6.221</p>
<p>   8     815     8.956	   818     8.993</p>
<p>   9     709  6200.000	   705  6164.000</p>
<p>  10    1178     5.950	  1181     5.964</p>
